117 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (Confidence Scores When the roberta-basego_emotions model analyzes user text, it doesn't just output one emotion. Instead, it generates a Probability Distribution across all 28 emotion categories. The Confidence Score is a percentage \(0.95 = 95%\) representing mathematical certainty. For example, if confidence is 0.95 for "Anger", the neural network is 95% certain that anger is the dominant emotion. This score is critical because it tells Gemini exactly how intense the user's emotion is, enabling more nuanced and appropriate responses. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 214 0 R
/T (Why Reinforcement Learning While the emotion detection and memory extraction are excellent, the generative responses from Gemini can still be improved. RLHF allows the system to learn from actual user feedback. Users rate responses as "Helpful" or "Not Helpful", creating a feedback loop that teaches the AI what kinds of responses are truly empathetic and effective for different emotional states.)
/E (Why Reinforcement Learning While the emotion detection and memory extraction are excellent, the generative responses from Gemini can still be improved. RLHF allows the system to learn from actual user feedback. Users rate responses as "Helpful" or "Not Helpful", creating a feedback loop that teaches the AI what kinds of responses are truly empathetic and effective for different emotional states.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 215 0 R
/T (Where RLHF is Applied RLHF is applied specifically to finetune the Gemini model's response generation. By collecting thousands of user feedback ratings alongside the exact emotional context \(emotion tags, confidence scores, memories, conversation history\), developers can train reward models that learn to predict which responses users find most helpful. These reward models then guide the fine-tuning of Gemini to generate increasingly empathetic and contextually appropriate responses.)
/E (Where RLHF is Applied RLHF is applied specifically to finetune the Gemini model's response generation. By collecting thousands of user feedback ratings alongside the exact emotional context \(emotion tags, confidence scores, memories, conversation history\), developers can train reward models that learn to predict which responses users find most helpful. These reward models then guide the fine-tuning of Gemini to generate increasingly empathetic and contextually appropriate responses.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
